It's quicker to adjust one stack onto another. This offers a few
benefits:

* Adjust merges all stacks of the selected item's type (i.e. it's not
limited
    to two stacks)
* It consumes no turns.
* It works when you're levitating over lava, etc.

I suppose dropping could offer the player more control in some
circumstances,
but I'm most certainly sticking with adjust. :)

